\[
f(n)=f(5k+r)=8(r-2)^5-(5k)^2+14\times 5k-24=8(r-2)^5-24
\]
When $r=0$, $8(r-2)^5-24=-8\times 32-24<0$ which is not a multiple of 5;
When $r=1$, $8(r-2)^5-24=-8-24<0$ which is not a multiple of 5;
When $r=2$, $8(r-2)^5-24=-24$ which is not a multiple of 5;
When $r=3$, $8(r-2)^5-24=8-24=-16$ which is not a multiple of 5;
When $r=4$, $8(r-2)^5-24=8\times 32-24=176=4 \bmod{5}$ which is not a multiple of 5;
Thus, when $n$ is not a multiple of 5, $f(n)$ cannot be a multiple of 5;
When $n$ is a multiple of 5, let $n=5k$, then we have:
\[
f(n)=f(5k)=8(5k-2)^5-(5k)^2+14\times 5k-24=8(5k-2)^5+5\times (14k-48)
\]
Since $f(n)$ equals a multiple of 5 plus a multiple of 5, $f(n)$ is a multiple of 5;
